          "For Account Research Source Decay Study, draw the stage 11 sample from a versioned eligible-record roster and report selected, available, unavailable, excluded, transferred, reopened, unresolved, suppressed, and late records separately. Two authorized reviewers independently label a planned reliability subset using the same codebook; calculate raw agreement and category-specific disagreement before adjudication. Freeze transformations in a reproducible query or worksheet, preserve nulls, and show how the result changes under declared denominator, timing, and inclusion alternatives. Do not describe association, reviewer agreement, or workflow timing as causation or a universal sales benchmark.",
          "Limitations. Account Research Source Decay Study stage 11 may be affected by missing events, changed policies, inconsistent clocks, selective documentation, seasonality, reviewer learning, unavailable messages, small subgroups, channel mix, and differences between sales systems. The study cannot establish causation, legal compliance, individual intent, worker performance, or a universal conversion rate. Protocol SRS-1013-05-11 requires reporting these boundaries beside the result, retaining unresolved classifications, and seeking qualified review before any operational change. Replication on a later frozen cohort is necessary before expanding the interpretation."
